.TH USAGE-MONITOR-FOR-CLAUDE 1 "" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usage-monitor-for-claude \- system tray monitor for Claude usage and quota limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usage-monitor-for-claude
.RI [ --config-dir " " PATH ]
.RI [ --verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usage-monitor-for-claude
puts an icon in the system tray showing how much of your Claude session and
weekly quotas is left. The icon carries the first quota's percentage over two
progress bars; clicking it opens a popup with the account, every configured
quota, and the installed Claude Code versions.
.PP
Usage is read through the credentials of a logged-in Claude Code installation,
so no separate sign-in is needed. Rate limits are shared across claude.ai,
Claude Code and the IDE extensions, so the figures cover all of them.
.PP
Only one instance runs per Claude configuration directory; starting a second
one for the same directory raises the popup of the running instance instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config-dir " PATH"
Monitor the Claude account configured in
.IR PATH
instead of the default
.IR ~/.claude .
Both
.BI --config-dir= PATH
and
.BI "--config-dir " PATH
are accepted;
.IR ~
and environment variables are expanded. Each configuration directory gets its
own settings, state and tray instance, so several accounts can be monitored at
once. The program exits with status 1 if the directory does not exist.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print startup diagnostics - resolved paths, settings source and detected Claude
installations - to standard output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/usage-monitor-settings.json
Optional settings file. It is never created automatically; see the
.B CONFIGURATION
section for the full search order.
.TP
.I ~/.config/usage-monitor-for-claude/state.json
Saved popup position and other persisted state. A non-default
.B --config-dir
adds a suffix to the file name.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/usage-monitor-for-claude.desktop
Written when "Start with system" is enabled from the tray menu.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The first of these that exists is used:
.IP 1. 4
.IR $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/usage-monitor-settings.json ,
when that variable is set and differs from
.IR ~/.claude .
.IP 2. 4
Next to the program, for tarball and portable installs.
.IP 3. 4
.I usage-monitor-settings.json
under
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/usage-monitor-for-claude ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/usage-monitor-for-claude .
.IP 4. 4
.IR ~/.claude/usage-monitor-settings.json .
.PP
Every user-tunable constant can be overridden there: polling intervals, colors,
which quotas the icon and popup show, alert thresholds, event commands and the
interface language. The settings reference lists them all.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Claude configuration directory to read credentials and usage from.
.B --config-dir
sets this for the process when given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination.
.TP
.B 1
The directory passed to
.B --config-dir
does not exist.
.SH SEE ALSO
Settings reference and full documentation:
.UR https://github.com/jorgealonsodev/usage-monitor-for-claude-linux
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Linux port by J. Alonso, from the Windows application by Jens Duttke.
